beat.com/feeds/5964598819898640914/comments/default" title="Post Comments" /><link rel="replies" type="text/html" href="https://www.borderlandbeat.com/2026/09/three-captured-after-cjng-car-bomb-in.html#comment-form" title="4 Comments" /><link rel="edit" type="application/atom+xml" href="https://www.blogger.com/feeds/5195137745759962560/posts/default/5964598819898640914" /><link rel="self" type="application/atom+xml" href="https://www.blogger.com/feeds/5195137745759962560/posts/default/5964598819898640914" /><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.borderlandbeat.com/2026/09/three-captured-after-cjng-car-bomb-in.html" title="Three Captured after CJNG Car Bomb in Ojocaliente, Zacatecas" /><author><name>El Huaso</name><uri>http://www.blogger.com/profile/15780051836540498633</uri><email>noreply@blogger.com</email><gd:image rel="http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#thumbnail" width="32" height="32" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEgTsKn_L5I6RhHI7c9rAs3hKtGfrTaKBEf0yN48KZIC6M-Ss5xAw9Y6oKSWFD_rsu0cdIaKFy2iyRuUCqnkzhUK23Cck4jkSh4SutzhCBgUkvbP82Vr3r4ago6oahv5c8_yozQY_Cqnapq54cz6xMDW-Yozi3OBKdYDS9smpkNasuLmCg/s1600/jABJEk3w_400x400.jpg" /></author><media:thumbnail url="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/a/AVvXsEgSTE1DIo9hhN2UaYbKUAjgvvuwJpHco8HJC9jM3rNjEiJhCu2DxgIq1oKRhKXOugbjzLd-NKA0-1Bzcu3ZSy9IU7H6fV0s1CQVYx9kS-EeNKKql1BB4ODBjG5heIgCufHlh-wJZ31gVWciSfoG6e3qgB2FDNOsI8bWPRvUDmYzrg8tQB6l_tr5MR42avy8=s72-c" height="72" width="72" /></entry><entry><id>tag:blogger.com,1999:blog-5195137745759962560.post-6146328201827243890</id><published>2026-08-31T23:11:59.826-06:00</published><updated>2026-08-31T23:11:59.826-06:00</updated><title type="text">Mexican Security Forces Kill Luis Enrique Barragán Chávez, a.k.a. “R5” and “Wicho de los Reyes”</title><content type="html">&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="background-color: white; color: #393b3e; font-family: Calibri; font-size: 10.5pt; letter-spacing: 0pt;"&gt;In the early morning of August 31, the Mexican Army, with support from the Secretariat of Security and Citizen Protection, conducted a security operation in the Sierra of Michoacán that resulted in the death of Luis Enrique Barragán Chávez, a.k.a. “R5” and “Wicho de los Reyes.”&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;span style="background: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: #393b3e; font-family: Calibri; font-size: 10.5pt; letter-spacing: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;span style="background: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: #393b3e; font-family: Calibri; font-size: 10.5pt; letter-spacing: 0pt;"&gt;&lt;i&gt;Who Was “R5”?&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;span style="background: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: #393b3e; font-family: Calibri; font-size: 10.5pt; letter-spacing: 0pt;"&gt;According to U.S. authorities, Luis Enrique Barragán Chávez was a regional leader and chief of hitmen (jefe de sicarios) for the Los Reyes Cartel. Barragán Chávez reportedly became involved in Michoacán's armed groups alongside his brother-in-law, with whom he initially fought Los Caballeros Temp</content><link rel="replies" type="application/atom+xml" href="https://www.borderlandbeat.com/feeds/6146328201827243890/comments/default" title="Post Comments" /><link rel="replies" type="text/html" href="https://www.borderlandbeat.com/2026/08/mexican-security-forces-kill-luis.html#comment-form" title="67 Comments" /><link rel="edit" type="application/atom+xml" href="https://www.blogger.com/feeds/5195137745759962560/posts/default/6146328201827243890" /><link rel="self" type="application/atom+xml" href="https://www.blogger.com/feeds/5195137745759962560/posts/default/6146328201827243890" /><link rel="alternate" type="text/html" href="https://www.borderlandbeat.com/2026/08/mexican-security-forces-kill-luis.html" title="Mexican Security Forces Kill Luis Enrique Barragán Chávez, a.k.a. “R5” and “Wicho de los Reyes”" /><author><name>KARAMAZOV</name><